From d165fa49d842eb28994e8189791f41b2f8fbce92 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: A2Tools-patch <patch@localhost>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 00:51:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 25/25] No A2 Tools services: the private build, with this
 fork's updates

This build reaches no service of the original and asks for no account:
it is built without `online`, the original's private build, which links
none of that code: the A2 Tools account and sign-in, sharing fights and
the leaderboards (the "Help build the leaderboards?" prompt), field boss
and supply reports, party presence, the shared boss timer feeds, the
plugin catalog, the supporter roster, Send Logs to Dev, Discord activity
and the stream overlay. The pages hide all of it (html.a2-offline).

A new feature `net` brings back the network client alone, for what this
fork reaches: its own releases (the update check, the updater) and the
web services plugins list (a2.web.get, the Market's prices). build_features
tells the pages `updates`, so the green button and Settings' update check
stay. The Arch package builds with `desktop,net`.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RahWACwaxzLAcYgwc9jk8C
